    <briefdescription>
<para>A type identity that stays comparable across shared library boundaries. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>libc++ compares <computeroutput>std::type_info</computeroutput> by address, and a type named from more than one shared library has one typeinfo per module once those modules are built with hidden visibility, as endstone and its plugins are. Comparing the mangled name instead lets a type named in a plugin match the same type named in the runtime. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
